# AY <-> VeriPB checker PIN. Single source of truth.
#
# Everything that verifies an AY proof — CI, `scripts/ci/pb_certified_gate.sh`,
# `scripts/cert_ci.sh`, and the Rust gates in `crates/ay-test-support/src/veripb.rs`
# (module `pin`, which `include_str!`s THIS file) and `crates/ay/src/maxsat_cert.rs`
# — reads the checker identity from here. There is no second copy to drift.
#
# WHY A PIN AT ALL. "VeriPB accepted it" only means something if you can say
# WHICH VeriPB. Upstream 3.0.2 as published has TWENTY-ONE confirmed wrong-verdict
# defects (see ci/veripb-soundness/README.md): it will print `s VERIFIED
# UNSATISFIABLE` for satisfiable formulas and `s VERIFIED SATISFIABLE` for
# unsatisfiable ones, given the right (small, non-adversarial-looking) proof.
# A green CI run against such a checker is not evidence. So the pin names an
# exact upstream commit PLUS one patch that fixes all twenty-one, and the gate
# re-proves the fixes on every run against committed fixtures before it trusts a
# verdict.
#
# HOW BAD IT GETS. Four of them need NOTHING from the formula, and two of those
# four contain no arithmetic anywhere. Defect 14 (order auxiliary variables are
# not order-private) forges `s VERIFIED UNSATISFIABLE` for an ARBITRARY
# satisfiable formula in four proof lines, by asserting an order's private
# variable TRUE at the top level and then letting `scope` inject the order's own
# specification — which says the opposite — as unconditional premises. Defect 15
# (the legacy version 2.0 parser enforces no rule scope) does the mirror image in
# six lines: `sol` inside an unterminated `pre_order` is checked against the
# ORDER's private empty database, so it "finds" a solution to a formula that has
# none and `conclusion SAT` publishes it. Defect 10
# (propagation slack computed in the row's own width) forges
# `s VERIFIED UNSATISFIABLE` against an ordinary satisfiable clause in three
# proof lines. Defect 11 (a proof-by-contradiction subproof FABRICATING a
# database proofgoal) does it in six, with no arithmetic anywhere and no extreme
# number in sight — and through checked deletion the same fabrication deletes a
# core constraint for free, forging `s VERIFIED SATISFIABLE` for an
# unsatisfiable formula. While either was open, no verdict from an unpatched
# 3.0.2 was evidence of anything for any formula. That is the standard this pin
# exists to hold: not "the checker is usually right", but "these exact wrong
# verdicts are re-proved impossible on every run".
#
# TWENTY-ONE DEFECTS, TWENTY-TWO FIXTURES. Keep both numbers in view; they are
# different things and conflating them is what made an earlier revision of this
# file say "six" when the audit said "eight". The defect count is TWENTY-ONE. The
# fixture count is TWENTY-TWO, because defect 7 (normalization wrapping) has two
# manifestations with OPPOSITE wrong verdicts and each needs its own pair. The
# mapping of the twenty-one defects to the twenty-two fixture directories is
# total:
#   1->01  2->02  3->03  4->04  5->09  6->05  7->07 and 08  8->06  9->10
#   10->11  11->12  12->13  13->14  14->15  15->16  16->17  17->18  18->19
#   19->20  20->21  21->22
#
# FORMAT: strict KEY=VALUE, no spaces, no quoting, no expansion. It is `.`-able
# from POSIX sh and parsed by a hand-written Rust reader; keep it boring.
#
# TO MOVE THE PIN (checker upgrade):
#   1. Rebase the fork's `alab-main` onto the new upstream commit, push it, and
#      re-cut VERIPB_PATCH as `git diff <upstream> <new-alab-main-tip>` from a
#      FRESH CLONE of the fork (see below). One patch, no second file.
#   2. Update VERIPB_COMMIT / VERIPB_VERSION / VERIPB_PATCH / VERIPB_PATCH_SHA256
#      here, and REWRITE THIS PROSE to match — the pin's history includes a
#      false-prose incident, so the words move with the value or not at all.
#   3. Run `scripts/ci/pb_certified_gate.sh`. It rebuilds from scratch, re-runs
#      the twenty-two soundness fixtures, and re-verifies every certified-track
#      proof. If the new checker regressed any of the twenty-two, the gate fails
#      and the upgrade does not land. That is the whole point: a checker swap
#      cannot change what "verified" means without turning CI red.

# Upstream repository the pinned checker is built from.
VERIPB_REPO=https://gitlab.com/MIAOresearch/software/VeriPB.git

# Exact upstream commit the patch is cut against. `--version` is NOT an
# identity: 3.0.2 has been many different checkers. The sha is the identity; the
# version is a cross-check. This is the shared base of the vendored veripb fork
# and upstream: the same commit, the same tree, on both sides, which is what
# lets the patch below be applied to a clean upstream checkout and reproduce
# the fork tip byte for byte.
VERIPB_COMMIT=4bb10c2ce98a8c80122a7a2399d7f35ffdc6e58e

# What the pinned build must report for `veripb --version` (last field).
VERIPB_VERSION=3.0.2

# ONE PATCH NOW. This repository previously carried TWO: VERIPB_PATCH was the
# byte-verified fork delta ending at f7f9d442 (eight wrong-verdict fixes plus the
# Clean-proved kernel), and VERIPB_PATCH2 was a fix written HERE for the
# remaining thirteen (defects 9-21). That split existed because the local fix had
# no byte-provenance in the fork and folding it into the fork delta would have
# destroyed the `cmp`-against-a-clone property of VERIPB_PATCH.
#
# THAT SPLIT IS GONE. 0002's thirteen fixes were ported onto the fork's
# `alab-main` (the defect-20 output-guarantee fix as a source change; defects
# 9-19 and 21 were already closed there by the fork's own wrong-verdict campaign,
# and their ay-side regression instances came over with it), and VERIPB_PATCH is
# re-cut from the new fork tip. So the fix for every one of the twenty-one
# defects now lives IN THE FORK, VERIPB_PATCH is once again a pure fork delta with
# nothing folded in, and VERIPB_PATCH2 is dropped in the same change per the
# procedure above. There is no file this repository edits in place any more: a
# further locally found defect is fixed in the fork and the patch re-cut, never
# added as a second numbered patch here.
#
# WHAT THE PATCH IS. The delta of the private fork branch `alab-main` ending at
# commit b1e80c0fe7e53ba79ad9e466d7a737823aedbbe9, over the shared upstream base
# VERIPB_COMMIT. It is `git diff --binary 4bb10c2c b1e80c0f` VERBATIM (the
# `--binary` is load-bearing: the fork added ten binary files after f7f9d442 —
# a `.cleancert` and nine compressed parser-test instances — that a text-only
# diff cannot carry). 601 files, +76944/-3084. Reproducible from public sources:
# clone the upstream repo, `git checkout 4bb10c2c`, `git apply` this patch,
# `cargo build --release --bin veripb`. Verified 2026-08-29 from a fresh clone
# of the fork at b1e80c0f: applying this patch to a clean 4bb10c2c checkout
# reproduces the fork tip's tree EXACTLY (`git write-tree` == b1e80c0f^{tree},
# `git diff b1e80c0f` empty).
#
# WHY THE FORK, NOT UPSTREAM. `alab-main` carries all twenty-one soundness fixes
# plus diagnostics and the Clean-proved kernel `veripb-core-proved`. Upstream
# 3.0.2 at 4bb10c2c has none of them. The three ay-authored reconciliation
# commits at the tip are:
#   88875e79  fix(soundness): output guarantees test the hazard, not the
#             solution_logged proxy   (defect 20; ported from the old 0002)
#   3510027c  test(soundness): port ay patch 0002's regression corpus for
#             defects 9-19, 21
#   b1e80c0f  chore(kernel-verify): re-bless coverage snapshot and census for
#             the ported instances
#
# KERNEL STATUS ON THIS BOX, STATED HONESTLY. `veripb-core-proved` is a
# workspace MEMBER that nothing depends on: `cargo build --bin veripb` does not
# compile it, and the shipped binary contains none of its symbols, so it decides
# NO verdict (the gate's phase 2b MEASURES that, it does not assume it). It is
# built and its tests are run on every gate invocation so it cannot rot. What the
# gate does NOT do is run `clean check` on the kernel proof itself, and here is
# why, measured on this box:
#
#   clean 1.2.0, from the `trust` stage3-tools-bin tree
#   (.../trust/build/aarch64-apple-darwin/stage3-tools-bin/
#   aarch64-apple-darwin/clean)
#     tip (b1e80c0f)  kernel: 874 declarations, 471 checked, 403 unchecked (rc 1)
#
# The gap is a TOOLCHAIN LINEAGE mismatch, not rotted proofs: `Nat.eq_of_beq_eq_true`
# does not exist in clean 1.2.0 under that or any probed alias, and one explicit
# `sorry` compatibility shim is present. The fork's own `scripts/verify-proofs.sh`
# checks the same kernel GREEN under the Clean lineage its pins name
# (`clean 0.1.0|v0.1.0-22-g...`, 77 suites), which is not present on this box.
# Until that toolchain is available here the kernel is UNVERIFIABLE on this box,
# and — exactly as when the pin sat at f7f9d442 — this gate makes NO claim about
# the kernel proof, only about the crate (that it compiles and its Rust tests
# pass). Do not read the kernel's presence as an increase in the trustworthiness
# of any existing certification claim. See ci/veripb-soundness/README.md.
VERIPB_PATCH=ci/veripb-patches/0001-ay-veripb-alab-main.patch
VERIPB_PATCH_SHA256=11d772ada406cc637979058c5d218b026ecb77c84713c2bda10938e1896c32a0

# Fixtures the pinned checker MUST reject (one directory per known bug).
VERIPB_SOUNDNESS_DIR=ci/veripb-soundness

# The certified-track instance set and its expected verdicts.
VERIPB_CERT_MANIFEST=ci/cert-instances/manifest.tsv
